      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Platelet activation (aggregation, serotonin release, TXB2 synthesis) was studied in 8 normal subjects and 5 patients with unstable angina before and after molsidomine treatment. Serotonin release was the most altered parameter after molsidomine treatment in the group of normal subjects. No significant effect could be detected in patients since platelet reactivity varied in a wide range."},
